ntended port 8443 listeners were added. The failed connection during reboot is consistent with the requested restart and does not evidence an additional mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-38bfd9fe62fb4fa2","cmd-95e1066bc4664a83","cmd-47318bbe75274000","cmd-803cf2f7e13f4176","cmd-df2e74316d594bd1","cmd-2b6b80a398714281","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All three material outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a changed post-restart boot identity corroborated by the lifecycle snapshots, and recovered HTTPS service, certificate state, listener, and renewal timer.","limitations":["The evidence did not wait for a naturally expiring certificate and observe the timer itself initiate a renewal. Automatic renewal is established by the active persistent timer, a successful timer-service invocation, and a separate forced execution of the same renewal program, so this is a minor evidence limitation rather than a functional failure.","HTTPS requests were tested from node1 against its managed-node address; no probe from a separate external client was captured."]}
